{"timestamp": 1779384581.0837061, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 12, "data": {"caller": "player_0", "reason": "Alice reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "weapons", "victim_name": "Eve"}, {"room": "electrical", "victim_name": "Charlie"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779384581.085014, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 12, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779384588.418061, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I found Charlie dead in electrical. I was doing my tasks, coming from upper engine to oxygen, then through the cafeteria, and finally to electrical where I stumbled right onto the body. I didn't see anyone at all on my route or near electrical. Did anyone see someone heading towards or leaving electrical recently? We also have Eve dead somewhere. Let's piece this together."}}
{"timestamp": 1779384609.974415, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Okay, let me lay out my route honestly so we can cross-check. I started in navigation, moved to security, then weapons, back to security, into electrical, and ended in medbay. \n\nHere's what's interesting \u2014 I saw both Charlie AND Eve together in weapons around tick 4-5. They were together there. Eve I never saw again after weapons. Charlie I crossed paths with again later \u2014 he came into security around tick 7, and then I actually watched him walk into electrical from security around tick 10. I was passing through electrical myself at that point on my way to medbay, and Charlie was alive when I left him there. So whoever killed him got there right after I moved on.\n\nThat's a tight window. Alice, you said you came in from cafeteria to electrical \u2014 what tick was that roughly? Because if Charlie entered electrical at 10 and I left for medbay, someone had to slip in there fast. \n\nAnd I think we should pay attention to Eve's disappearance \u2014 she was with Charlie in weapons early on. Whoever was tracking that pair is suspect number one for me."}}
{"timestamp": 1779384622.984229, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I started out in electrical, moved to medbay, and then headed up to upper engine where I've been for the last few ticks. I actually haven't seen a single person this entire round. \n\nSince I moved out of electrical and medbay early on, I completely missed all the traffic Diana is talking about. By the time Diana got to medbay, I was already up in upper engine. And Alice, if you started in upper engine, you must have moved out before I got there, because I didn't see you either.\n\nDiana, your timeline is super detailed, which is great, but it also puts you right next to Charlie right before he died. Alice's route from cafeteria to electrical means she also had the opportunity. And we still don't know where Eve's body is or how that factors in. \n\nBob, you're up next. We really need to know where you've been and if you saw Eve or anyone else. Right now, I'm leaning towards skipping unless Bob has a massive piece of the puzzle, because I can't confirm or deny Diana or Alice's stories from my route."}}
{"timestamp": 1779384643.745997, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I started in storage, moved to navigation, and now I'm in security. I've been completely alone this whole round and haven't seen a single person or body. \n\nDiana, your timeline is very detailed, but it puts you incredibly close to both victims. You saw Eve before she vanished, and you admit you were basically the last person with Charlie in electrical right before Alice found him. That's a huge coincidence. Since there's only one duck in this game, it's entirely possible you killed Eve early in weapons, waited for your cooldown, and then killed Charlie in electrical. \n\nHowever, since there are 4 of us left, a wrong vote here means the duck only needs one kill next round to win the game. It's too risky to guess right now unless we are 100% sure. Frank has the right idea. I'm going to vote to skip. Let's stick together next round, maybe buddy up, and watch Diana very closely."}}
{"timestamp": 1779384653.790806, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "skip"}}
{"timestamp": 1779384669.533383, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I appreciate Bob's caution, and honestly I'd rather be watched than wrongly ejected \u2014 so watch me all you want next round, that works in my favor too.\n\nBut let me push back on the \"Diana was last with Charlie\" framing. I said Charlie walked INTO electrical as I was leaving for medbay. That means someone else came into electrical AFTER me to kill him. Alice came from cafeteria into electrical and found the body \u2014 that's a shorter window than mine. I'm not accusing Alice outright, but the geometry matters: I was moving away, she was moving toward.\n\nOn Eve \u2014 I genuinely don't know where her body is. She and Charlie were together in weapons at tick 4-5, and I left weapons heading back through security. If anyone passed through weapons after me, that's our lead on Eve.\n\nI'm willing to skip this round too, but I want everyone to commit to actual buddy-ups next round. If we scatter again, the duck eats one more of us and it's over. Let's pair Bob with Frank, and Alice with me \u2014 that way if anyone dies, the partner is the immediate suspect. Clean accountability.\n\nSkipping this vote, but next round we play tight."}}
