{"timestamp": 1779384925.5329568, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 25, "data": {"caller": "player_5", "reason": "Frank reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "storage", "victim_name": "Alice"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779384925.53423, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 25, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779384939.83628, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 25, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I just found Alice dead in storage. Guys, this is it\u2014it's just me, Bob, and Diana left. Since there's only three of us and one Duck, if we guess wrong here, it's game over. \n\nMy route this round was oxygen, then cafeteria, over to weapons, back through cafeteria, down to medbay, and finally into storage where I walked in on the body. The crazy part is I didn't see a single soul this entire round until I found Alice. \n\nBob, Diana, I need to hear exactly where you both were, your exact routes, and if you saw each other. One of you is the Duck, so whoever's story has holes is getting my vote. Please be detailed."}}
{"timestamp": 1779384963.577821, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 25, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Okay Frank, full transparency since this is the make-or-break round.\n\nMy route was lower engine, then storage, then navigation, then security, and I ended in weapons. I was doing tasks the whole way through \u2014 wiring in security, the asteroid panel in weapons.\n\nHere's the important part: I was in storage around tick 16, and Alice was alive in there with me. We didn't really interact, I just passed through and headed to navigation. So if Frank found her dead in storage later, that means someone came in AFTER I left.\n\nFrank, you said your route was oxygen \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 weapons \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 medbay \u2192 storage. That's a long loop, and storage was your LAST stop. That timing actually works \u2014 Alice could have been killed between when I left her and when you arrived.\n\nBut here's what bothers me: Bob, where the hell were you? I didn't see you ONCE this entire round. Not in lower engine, not in storage, not in nav, not in security, not in weapons. Frank didn't see you either. In a 6-player game down to 3, that's wild. You've been a ghost both rounds.\n\nI also saw Charlie at weapons around tick 4, then security at tick 7, then electrical at tick 10 \u2014 and Eve was at weapons ticks 4-5. So early game I had eyes on people. After tick 10 though, everyone vanished except Alice in storage.\n\nBob, give us your exact route. If you say you were anywhere near storage in the back half of the round, you're the Duck. I'm voting Bob unless his route somehow accounts for never crossing paths with either of us."}}
{"timestamp": 1779384987.194452, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 25, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "\"Frank, I caught you in a massive lie, and you just handed us the game. \n\nYou claimed your route this round was Oxygen -> Cafeteria -> Weapons -> Cafeteria -> Medbay -> Storage. \n\nWell, my exact route this round was Weapons -> Cafeteria -> Oxygen -> Upper Engine. We literally took the exact same path in reverse. If you actually went from Oxygen to Cafeteria to Weapons, we would have 100% crossed paths or seen each other in Cafeteria. But I didn't see a single soul up there the entire round, and you just admitted you didn't see anyone either. \n\nYou completely made up that northern route to give yourself a fake alibi, not realizing I was actually up there the whole time! You probably killed Alice in Storage, waited, and self-reported, or you were lurking near the bottom of the map the whole time.\n\nDiana, vote Frank with me. His route is mathematically impossible without us seeing each other. He's the Duck.\""}}
{"timestamp": 1779384997.945642, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 25, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Bob"}}
{"timestamp": 1779385030.19646, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 25, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Bob, your \"gotcha\" sounds clever but it's actually full of holes \u2014 and it's making me lean hard toward you.\n\nFirst, routes don't have to overlap in time just because they share rooms. Frank could have been in cafeteria at tick 6 while you were there at tick 14. You're treating \"same room\" like a contradiction when it's really just a timing question. That's a classic Duck misdirection move \u2014 make a confident-sounding logic claim that doesn't actually hold up.\n\nSecond, look at where your route ENDS: Upper Engine. From Upper Engine you have a direct 2-tick corridor to Lower Engine, and Lower Engine connects straight to Storage. So if you \"ended\" in Upper Engine in the front half of the round, you had all the time in the world to slip down to Storage through the back stairs and kill Alice after I left her there at tick 16. Your route conveniently stops right before the kill window.\n\nThird \u2014 and this is the big one \u2014 Frank's northern loop matches my early-game sightings. I saw Charlie and Eve at weapons ticks 4-5, then Charlie moved to security and electrical. Frank says he was bouncing through cafeteria and weapons. That's consistent with the foot traffic I observed up north. Your claim that \"no one was up there\" directly contradicts what I saw with my own eyes.\n\nFrank found the body. I was demonstrably doing tasks on the east and south side. You're the one with the unaccounted-for back half of the round and a route that puts you one corridor away from Storage.\n\nI'm voting Bob."}}
{"timestamp": 1779385047.055787, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 25, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Diana, you are making a massive mistake and handing the game to Frank. Yes, I ended my route in Upper Engine, but I was literally stuck there doing the Align Engine Output task. I never went down to Lower Engine or Storage \u2014 I've been top-left the entire back half of the round. \n\nThink about it: Frank says he went Cafeteria -> Medbay -> Storage. You said you left Alice in Storage around tick 16. Frank's route conveniently places him walking into Storage right at the end of the round to \"find\" the body. He killed her and self-reported because it's final 3 and he knew he could just point fingers. \n\nMy route doesn't contradict your early sightings because I was in Weapons at the very start of the round before anyone else got there, and I moved west while everyone else was east. Frank is playing you. If you vote me, the game is over and the Geese lose. Please, vote Frank!"}}
